1
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:24,065
Soo-hyun!

2
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:26,693
You bastard!

3
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:28,319
Hey! Shit!

4
00:00:29,821 --> 00:00:32,407
Hey, man! Soo-hyun!

5
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,075
Hey! I just wanna talk!

6
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:37,370
Soo-hyun!

7
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:39,122
Just talk to me for a second!

8
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:40,874
Hey!

9
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:42,876
- Soo-hyun!
- Huh?

10
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:44,919
- Soo-hyun, talk to me! Stop!
- What the hell?

11
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:46,880
Soo-hyun. You punk!

12
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:48,256
Soo-hyun!

13
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:49,466
Hey!

14
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:50,800
I said let's talk, man.

15
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:52,761
Where are you going? Hey!

16
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:54,763
What's wrong with you? Let's just talk!

17
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:55,680
Open up for a sec.

18
00:00:56,264 --> 00:00:57,724
Hey!

19
00:00:57,807 --> 00:01:00,101
Just talk to me, you bastard!

20
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:02,854
Look at me. Soo-hyun! Goddamn it!

21
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:04,856
Hey! Stop the car!

22
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:08,234
Wait. Just a second.

23
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:09,402
Just a sec, Soo-hyun!

24
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:10,403
Just talk to me.

25
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:12,322
Wait! Hey!

26
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:14,074
Hey! Don't go, man!

27
00:01:18,495 --> 00:01:19,370
Get in, you idiot!

28
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:22,332
What the hell are you doing
yelling "Soo-hyun" over there?

29
00:01:22,415 --> 00:01:23,333
Shit!

30
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:42,310
Damn it.

31
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:32,193
MOUSETRAP

32
00:02:56,968 --> 00:02:58,178
That little…

33
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:33,713
JE MOON-JAE

34
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:35,590
Hey, Moon-jae.

35
00:03:36,216 --> 00:03:38,384
<i>It was a trap. A damn trap!</i>

36
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:39,427
They're on my tail!

37
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:47,852
<i>You said you'd let us live</i>
<i>if I did what you said!</i>

38
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:49,520
- You gonna do what I say?
- What?

39
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:54,776
<i>I can't hear you!</i>

40
00:03:55,276 --> 00:03:56,861
You're supposed to do what I say.

41
00:04:13,878 --> 00:04:15,713
What the hell are they doing?

42
00:04:15,797 --> 00:04:17,340
And who the hell are they chasing?

43
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:33,231
<i>What if only one of you can live?</i>

44
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:35,483
<i>Soo-hyun.</i>

45
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:38,903
<i>I don't think both of you can live.</i>

46
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:41,197
<i>Hello?</i>

47
00:04:45,410 --> 00:04:46,828
One of you should live.

48
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:48,746
<i>Don't you think?</i>

49
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:56,254
- <i>What's the matter, sir?</i>
- Hey, kid.

50
00:04:56,337 --> 00:04:58,339
I'm chasing someone.

51
00:04:58,423 --> 00:04:59,882
I might need your help--

52
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:05,763
<i>Hello?</i>

53
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:07,515
<i>Sir?</i>

54
00:05:08,474 --> 00:05:09,475
<i>Hello?</i>

55
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:13,438
<i>Sir!</i>

56
00:05:18,109 --> 00:05:19,193
Soo-hyun!

57
00:05:20,653 --> 00:05:22,697
Soo-hyun! Just pull over!

58
00:05:24,073 --> 00:05:25,033
Hey, bastard!

59
00:05:25,116 --> 00:05:26,868
Soo-hyun! Pull over! Hey!

60
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:28,536
Soo-hyun! Let's just talk! Hey!

61
00:05:28,619 --> 00:05:29,787
Soo-hyun!

62
00:05:38,254 --> 00:05:39,714
We have to stop him! He'll die.

63
00:05:39,797 --> 00:05:41,924
- Huh?
- He's gonna kill himself!

64
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:08,451
Hey, Soo-hyun.

65
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:09,494
Soo-hyun!

66
00:06:11,954 --> 00:06:12,789
What?

67
00:06:16,417 --> 00:06:17,794
Noja.

68
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:20,963
Hey, that bastard…

69
00:06:23,591 --> 00:06:24,509
Soo-hyun.

70
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:25,968
Hey, Soo-hyun!

71
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:27,178
- Get down, punk!
- Hey!

72
00:06:27,261 --> 00:06:28,888
- Hey, get down!
- Get down!

73
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:29,806
Get down.

74
00:06:31,432 --> 00:06:32,600
Get down. What are you…

75
00:06:32,683 --> 00:06:34,477
Get a hold of yourself!

76
00:06:42,318 --> 00:06:44,070
He called himself "The Rat."

77
00:06:45,279 --> 00:06:46,781
He said he knows you well.

78
00:06:46,864 --> 00:06:47,824
Okay. Just get down.

79
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:50,159
Who's the Rat? Who's that bastard?

80
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:52,662
He's Moon-jae.

81
00:06:52,745 --> 00:06:54,163
For fuck's sake.

82
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,081
Je Moon-jae.

83
00:06:55,998 --> 00:06:57,625
Hey, I'm Je Moon-jae--

84
00:06:57,708 --> 00:07:01,504
Fuck, I don't even know
who the real Moon-jae is anymore.

85
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:05,049
- Hey, it's been a long time.
- Been a while, Soo-hyun.

86
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:06,175
See you inside.

87
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:12,807
<i>It was around this time last year</i>
<i>when I first met him.</i>

88
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:14,725
Shit, what's that bastard doing here?

89
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:17,103
Hey, what are you doing here?

90
00:07:17,186 --> 00:07:18,271
Hey, Soo-hyun.

91
00:07:18,354 --> 00:07:19,272
You're here.

92
00:07:19,355 --> 00:07:20,898
<i>He even knew my name.</i>

93
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:23,192
He knew everything about us.

94
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:27,113
I need some money.

95
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:30,241
The money you guys stole.

96
00:07:30,741 --> 00:07:32,743
He even threatened
to report us to the police

97
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:36,247
for skimming the investment funds.

98
00:07:36,330 --> 00:07:39,041
I have a family.
I had no choice but to do what he said.

99
00:07:40,501 --> 00:07:42,170
After all,

100
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:44,130
we're both frauds.

101
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:47,675
Yeah.

102
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:49,677
You're right. Just get down.

103
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,262
Get down. Then we'll talk.

104
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:52,221
Who is he?

105
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:54,557
Just tell me who he is. Okay?

106
00:07:57,727 --> 00:08:00,563
Then he suddenly told me
to bring your phone.

107
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:17,872
<i>He said he'd been preparing</i>
<i>for a long time.</i>

108
00:08:18,539 --> 00:08:21,209
<i>He even changed his face and voice</i>

109
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:24,003
<i>to take everything you've got.</i>

110
00:08:24,962 --> 00:08:26,088
Didn't I tell you?

111
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:27,840
Everything was planned.

112
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:31,177
The phone, the broken glass…

113
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:32,970
Maybe even Da-eun's kidnapping.

114
00:08:33,721 --> 00:08:36,516
When I hesitated to pay him,
he kidnapped Da-eun.

115
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:38,351
He said he'd kill her if I got caught.

116
00:08:38,434 --> 00:08:39,936
Exactly. Come on.

117
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:42,605
Just think of Da-eun, okay?

118
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:43,773
Come down.

119
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:45,691
- Shit.
- Goddamn it!

120
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:48,819
I just had to hold out a little longer.

121
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:52,448
He said he'd let Da-eun go soon.

122
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:55,785
Fuck. Then it would've been all over.

123
00:08:55,868 --> 00:08:56,827
You're right.

124
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:58,829
Hey, it's all over.

125
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:00,915
Get a hold of yourself! You…

126
00:09:00,998 --> 00:09:03,459
Soo-hyun.
Let's catch that bastard together. Okay?

127
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:05,628
We can catch that bastard together.

128
00:09:05,711 --> 00:09:07,046
It's all over. Fuck.

129
00:09:07,129 --> 00:09:09,590
The moment I don't do as I'm told,

130
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:11,634
Da-eun dies.

131
00:09:12,885 --> 00:09:15,763
You have no idea
how scary that bastard is.

132
00:09:15,846 --> 00:09:18,182
So who the hell is that bastard?

133
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:19,517
Who is he? Just tell me.

134
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:21,769
There's gotta be a reason he's doing this!

135
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:24,647
Yes. That's it.

136
00:09:26,232 --> 00:09:27,984
He said you'd know why.

137
00:09:29,318 --> 00:09:30,194
Me?

138
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:32,780
You said the broken window
was a bug, right?

139
00:09:33,781 --> 00:09:35,116
Yeah, it was a bug.

140
00:09:35,199 --> 00:09:37,368
Because that bastard's a bug in our lives.

141
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:41,414
This is all…

142
00:09:44,166 --> 00:09:45,376
because of your lies.

143
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:51,215
We're screwed, you bastard.

144
00:09:54,343 --> 00:09:55,428
What lies…

145
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:57,763
- Huh?
- Grab him!

146
00:09:57,847 --> 00:09:58,848
Grab him!

147
00:10:07,898 --> 00:10:09,108
Fuck!

148
00:10:09,191 --> 00:10:10,484
Hey!

149
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:14,864
Fuck!

150
00:10:29,003 --> 00:10:29,837
Turn around.

151
00:10:35,926 --> 00:10:37,053
Fuck!

152
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:45,269
"Lies"? What the hell did he mean,
you punk?

153
00:10:47,521 --> 00:10:48,356
What?

154
00:10:51,942 --> 00:10:54,528
<i>Let's say you're the captain</i>
<i>of a passenger plane.</i>

155
00:10:55,529 --> 00:10:57,948
You're flying a plane full of passengers,

156
00:10:58,449 --> 00:11:00,660
when you realize there's a malfunction.

157
00:11:02,119 --> 00:11:03,537
A critical malfunction.

158
00:11:06,123 --> 00:11:07,875
Beyond repair.

159
00:11:07,958 --> 00:11:09,585
Then what would you do?

160
00:11:10,086 --> 00:11:13,047
Would you tell the passengers
the plane's going to crash?

161
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:16,342
Or would you keep it a secret

162
00:11:17,176 --> 00:11:18,969
and just let it crash?

163
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:20,971
Is something wrong?

164
00:11:23,307 --> 00:11:26,227
When we met again after graduating,

165
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:29,188
you'd changed so much,
I didn't even recognize you.

166
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:37,321
Never mind. Heavy rain tomorrow.
Don't forget your umbrella.

167
00:11:38,406 --> 00:11:39,281
Right.

168
00:11:41,158 --> 00:11:43,077
You wouldn't need an umbrella.

169
00:11:51,419 --> 00:11:54,338
He could've given us his phone
before he died.

170
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:57,299
So it'd at least be easier
to find the bastard.

171
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:04,348
- Let's go to the police station, Noja.
- To do what?

172
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:06,600
Report him? Or turn yourself in?

173
00:12:06,684 --> 00:12:08,436
Either way.

174
00:12:09,895 --> 00:12:11,188
A man just died.

175
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:13,274
And his kid was kidnapped.

176
00:12:13,774 --> 00:12:15,025
We can't handle this.

177
00:12:15,693 --> 00:12:16,819
What about the money?

178
00:12:19,029 --> 00:12:19,864
Noja.

179
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:22,533
A man just died in front of us.

180
00:12:23,033 --> 00:12:24,702
Does money even matter right now?

181
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:30,666
A man just died over money.
So money matters more than people.

182
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:36,964
You bastard.

183
00:12:37,715 --> 00:12:39,175
Don't do that.

184
00:12:40,801 --> 00:12:42,553
I don't even have full coverage.

185
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:45,264
Even the police won't believe you.

186
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:46,932
How will you prove it?

187
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:50,352
You're not Je Moon-jae anymore.
And I'm just a thug.

188
00:12:51,562 --> 00:12:53,939
We'll have to handle this.

189
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:58,319
Because that rat bastard
is our only proof.

190
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:27,306
What are you doing here?

191
00:13:28,265 --> 00:13:29,725
Smoking.

192
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:35,105
You could've called a tow truck.
Why me? I worked all night.

193
00:13:35,689 --> 00:13:37,525
Because I missed you, you bastard.

194
00:13:39,235 --> 00:13:40,069
Why are you here?

195
00:13:40,152 --> 00:13:43,030
I don't even know what kind of shit
I've gotten myself into.

196
00:13:43,113 --> 00:13:43,948
Hey.

197
00:13:48,452 --> 00:13:49,578
Are you okay?

198
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:53,791
DONGBU POLICE STATION

199
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:02,591
So what is it?

200
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:05,135
You've got nothing? Huh?

201
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:08,430
You don't know where they went,
and you wrecked your car for nothing.

202
00:14:09,557 --> 00:14:12,434
So what's this case about?

203
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:14,979
I don't know. I'll have to find out.

204
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:16,605
Take the toothbrush out.

205
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:18,899
You were probably goofing off, you punk.

206
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:21,694
I said I'll have to find out.

207
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:24,071
You told me to follow up on the tip,
so I did.

208
00:14:24,154 --> 00:14:26,073
And I ended up wrecking my car!

209
00:14:26,156 --> 00:14:28,158
Are you gonna reimburse me for it?

210
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:30,119
- You fucking won't!
- You bastard!

211
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:32,079
I almost fucking died doing my job!

212
00:14:32,162 --> 00:14:34,957
Give me shit again,
and I'm fucking quitting.

213
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,500
- Yeah, go ahead!
- Move!

214
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:37,459
Quit, you bastard.

215
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:39,336
Sun-yong! Just quit already.

216
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:40,921
Where do you think you're going?

217
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:43,340
- Sir, calm down.
- He's so fucking rude.

218
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:46,260
He might be tangled up
in more than one complicated case.

219
00:14:47,511 --> 00:14:48,470
That's what he said.

220
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:54,059
Learn from him, okay?

221
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,395
He's not one to bark up the wrong tree.

222
00:15:27,801 --> 00:15:28,969
"So Min-yeong."

223
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:32,473
Do these belong to the one in the morgue?

224
00:15:33,849 --> 00:15:34,683
Yes.

225
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,611
Move the operation now.

226
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:47,988
We need more identities.
Check Seoul Station again.

227
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:50,366
Yes, sir.

228
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:53,327
Watch Noja.

229
00:15:53,911 --> 00:15:54,787
- Yes, sir.
- Got it.

230
00:15:56,038 --> 00:15:56,956
Get home safe.

231
00:16:07,549 --> 00:16:10,844
The police came to the daycare
because of the kidnapping.

232
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:12,930
They didn't come for us.

233
00:16:13,013 --> 00:16:14,765
Our police are good at what they do.

234
00:16:14,848 --> 00:16:18,477
They'll find your friend's daughter,
even if we don't.

235
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:22,189
You try to figure out who the Rat is.

236
00:16:22,272 --> 00:16:23,315
Okay?

237
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:25,734
Before your friend jumped off,

238
00:16:26,235 --> 00:16:29,822
he said you'd know
why the Rat bastard is doing…

239
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:51,010
I definitely locked the door
before I left.

240
00:16:54,388 --> 00:16:55,264
Noja.

241
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:00,978
What is that?

242
00:17:01,645 --> 00:17:03,063
418-3 HWASAN-RI, GANGSANG-MYEON

243
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:24,334
This is the right address.

244
00:17:27,796 --> 00:17:29,882
What on earth could be here?

245
00:17:29,965 --> 00:17:31,091
Let's see what's here.

246
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:36,907
SON DA-EUN

247
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:34,715
Sir. The team leader's looking for you.

248
00:19:37,634 --> 00:19:38,510
What now?

249
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:40,179
Backup for another precinct.

250
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:41,096
It's a Code Zero.

251
00:19:48,353 --> 00:19:50,772
Abducted a week ago.
Reported yesterday by her mom.

252
00:19:50,856 --> 00:19:52,774
- And--
- A week ago?

253
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:54,443
She should've reported it sooner.

254
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:56,195
- Why did she wait?
- I don't know!

255
00:19:57,154 --> 00:19:59,948
The thing is, the dad's missing too.

256
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:01,867
Guess we should go get briefed.

257
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:05,954
Oh man, seriously. Shit.

258
00:20:08,665 --> 00:20:10,000
Yes, hello?

259
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:11,877
Yes.

260
00:20:12,836 --> 00:20:13,754
What?

261
00:20:16,173 --> 00:20:17,090
I see.

262
00:20:17,174 --> 00:20:18,550
Understood.

263
00:20:21,678 --> 00:20:23,096
481-3 HWASAN-RI, GANGSANG-MYEON

264
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,514
They found the girl.

265
00:20:24,598 --> 00:20:26,099
Thank God. Damn.

266
00:20:26,183 --> 00:20:28,393
Kill the siren. Take it slow.

267
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:39,863
Goddamn it.

268
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:41,198
They're coming.

269
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:45,244
Man, this place screams psycho.

270
00:20:45,327 --> 00:20:47,955
- Don't go in there.
- Yes, I'll lock it down.

271
00:20:49,206 --> 00:20:51,500
- This is a crime scene.
- Sure.

272
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:54,503
The suspect rented this place short-term.

273
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:58,340
They'll take the kidnapping case.
We'll handle the father's disappearance.

274
00:20:58,423 --> 00:21:01,301
So many cases in a country this small.

275
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:02,678
Yeah.

276
00:21:04,429 --> 00:21:05,847
What's that?

277
00:21:05,931 --> 00:21:06,807
Oh, this?

278
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:08,892
It's a CCTV image of the suspect.

279
00:21:13,814 --> 00:21:14,648
Hey.

280
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,441
Where's the kid now?

281
00:21:18,151 --> 00:21:20,696
Don't worry. We called the police.

282
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:22,155
She'll be fine.

283
00:21:22,239 --> 00:21:24,908
The cops must be swarming there by now.

284
00:21:24,992 --> 00:21:27,494
But where do we find this vicious bastard?

285
00:21:35,210 --> 00:21:36,211
Hey.

286
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:38,547
What now? Another panic attack?

287
00:21:39,047 --> 00:21:41,675
Noja. That's not the issue anymore.

288
00:21:42,592 --> 00:21:44,261
Soo-hyun was right.

289
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:47,973
I think we're screwed.

290
00:22:02,404 --> 00:22:03,447
Where is she?

291
00:22:05,866 --> 00:22:06,992
Is she here?

292
00:22:08,076 --> 00:22:09,161
Maybe that man…

293
00:22:09,244 --> 00:22:10,412
Is that the rescued kid?

294
00:22:10,495 --> 00:22:12,164
Yes. Where are you from?

295
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:13,206
Hey.

296
00:22:13,290 --> 00:22:15,709
- Hey, kid. Was it this man?
- Who are you?

297
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:17,377
- Do you know him?
- What's with you?

298
00:22:17,461 --> 00:22:18,754
- Just wait!
- Get out.

299
00:22:18,837 --> 00:22:20,130
Wait! Let go!

300
00:22:20,213 --> 00:22:21,548
- Stop!
- Did he scare you?

301
00:22:21,631 --> 00:22:24,051
- Let go of me!
- It was this person.

302
00:22:25,677 --> 00:22:27,346
Do you know him?

303
00:22:45,572 --> 00:22:47,199
Mister.

304
00:22:48,492 --> 00:22:49,868
Where's my mom?

305
00:22:57,834 --> 00:22:59,920
A guy who looks exactly like me
kidnapped her.

306
00:23:00,003 --> 00:23:01,213
What does that mean?

307
00:23:02,756 --> 00:23:04,466
You're the fucking kidnapper.

308
00:23:05,258 --> 00:23:06,718
Fucking hell. I'm losing it.

309
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:09,221
If there's a CCTV at the daycare…

310
00:23:09,304 --> 00:23:11,598
Fuck. That makes me an accomplice.

311
00:23:12,099 --> 00:23:13,683
And a murderer.

312
00:23:14,351 --> 00:23:15,560
If they find Soo-hyun…

313
00:23:16,186 --> 00:23:17,687
For fuck's sake.

314
00:23:18,355 --> 00:23:20,357
He's pinning it all on us.

315
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:21,274
It's all planned.

316
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:24,194
Hey, think this through.
Anyone hold a grudge against you?

317
00:23:24,277 --> 00:23:26,780
- Enough to get surgery to look like you.
- I don't know!

318
00:23:29,116 --> 00:23:30,575
I don't know.

319
00:23:30,659 --> 00:23:33,161
- Who could it be?
- Who else? It's you, bastard.

320
00:23:36,164 --> 00:23:37,374
We need to lay low.

321
00:23:37,457 --> 00:23:41,044
This is a fucked-up game
where you have to find yourself.

322
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:50,637
So,

323
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:53,974
you're saying the tip and the kidnapping
are the same case?

324
00:23:54,474 --> 00:23:56,184
- Who knows?
- What?

325
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:58,353
Wait. Hang on a minute.

326
00:23:58,437 --> 00:24:00,355
Who's that bastard with Noja?

327
00:24:00,439 --> 00:24:01,731
I don't know his name yet.

328
00:24:02,482 --> 00:24:04,651
You said you met him
when you went to his place.

329
00:24:04,734 --> 00:24:08,905
I didn't ask back then.
I was there to find Kim Yeong-geun, Noja.

330
00:24:09,656 --> 00:24:11,533
Hey! What kind of half-assed job is that?

331
00:24:11,616 --> 00:24:12,993
- Sir.
- Look.

332
00:24:13,076 --> 00:24:15,704
You met the suspect and let him walk.

333
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:19,082
You think suspects wear a fucking name tag
on their forehead?

334
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:20,417
This bastard.

335
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:23,336
Hey, learn to admit when you're wrong.

336
00:24:23,420 --> 00:24:25,172
Admit what? You crazy bastard!

337
00:24:25,255 --> 00:24:27,799
Stop fighting already, fucking bastards!

338
00:24:30,844 --> 00:24:31,678
You.

339
00:24:32,179 --> 00:24:34,181
They'd better be the same case. Or else…

340
00:24:35,724 --> 00:24:37,809
Hey. Learn from him, okay?

341
00:24:37,893 --> 00:24:39,853
Why are you taking it out on me?

342
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:44,441
Put this in there.

343
00:24:44,524 --> 00:24:45,734
Goddamn it.

344
00:24:45,817 --> 00:24:48,778
This is all we've got now.
We can't use our cards anymore.

345
00:24:50,322 --> 00:24:51,781
Take these, will you?

346
00:24:52,657 --> 00:24:53,700
Goddamn it.

347
00:24:55,494 --> 00:24:57,454
- I'm--
- We need to get out of here.

348
00:24:58,038 --> 00:25:00,999
- What the hell are you doing?
- I swear to God! Just wait.

349
00:25:01,082 --> 00:25:03,043
Back off.
I'm about to have a panic attack.

350
00:25:03,126 --> 00:25:04,544
Panic attack? Whatever.

351
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:06,713
Cops are quick, you bastard!

352
00:25:07,297 --> 00:25:08,381
You're so fucking slow.

353
00:25:16,973 --> 00:25:18,475
Hey, Chang-u. Go.

354
00:25:19,434 --> 00:25:20,560
See you later.

355
00:25:36,409 --> 00:25:37,285
Are they here?

356
00:25:42,207 --> 00:25:43,124
"They just left."

357
00:25:44,668 --> 00:25:45,669
What?

358
00:25:46,336 --> 00:25:47,712
Hey, is that him?

359
00:25:51,633 --> 00:25:53,677
Fuck, they're already here.

360
00:25:53,760 --> 00:25:55,512
- Huh? They're leaving.
- Crap. Hurry!

361
00:25:55,595 --> 00:25:56,513
Hey, let's go.

362
00:25:58,515 --> 00:25:59,474
- Stop them!
- Hey!

363
00:25:59,558 --> 00:26:00,392
Hey! Stop them!

364
00:26:00,475 --> 00:26:01,893
- Hurry!
- Hey, stop!

365
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:04,896
- Run! Damn it.
- Hey, you!

366
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:06,606
Get out!

367
00:26:08,817 --> 00:26:09,901
- Hey!
- Damn it.

368
00:26:09,985 --> 00:26:11,111
They're going that way!

369
00:26:11,194 --> 00:26:12,654
- Hey!
- Get them!

370
00:26:12,737 --> 00:26:13,905
Get them already!

371
00:26:23,915 --> 00:26:25,000
Hey!

372
00:26:25,542 --> 00:26:26,835
Stop right there!

373
00:26:27,836 --> 00:26:29,212
- Stop!
- Look! He fell!

374
00:26:29,296 --> 00:26:30,964
- Over there!
- Let's go!

375
00:26:31,047 --> 00:26:32,507
- Stop right there!
- Hey!

376
00:26:32,591 --> 00:26:34,092
- Hey!
- You fucking bastard!

377
00:26:34,175 --> 00:26:35,552
You fucking bastard!

378
00:26:35,635 --> 00:26:37,095
- Go that way!
- Hey!

379
00:26:37,178 --> 00:26:38,847
- Fucking hell!
- Hey!

380
00:26:39,764 --> 00:26:41,600
Stop! Hey, you!

381
00:26:46,771 --> 00:26:48,106
Hey! Stop, you bastard!

382
00:26:48,189 --> 00:26:49,316
Hey, you bastard!

383
00:26:49,399 --> 00:26:50,483
Stop right there!

384
00:26:51,359 --> 00:26:53,194
- Hey!
- Sir!

385
00:26:54,112 --> 00:26:54,946
Stop! Damn it!

386
00:26:55,030 --> 00:26:56,573
You bastard! Hey!

387
00:26:57,157 --> 00:26:59,200
- Go around.
- He's going over the wall!

388
00:26:59,284 --> 00:27:01,119
- He went over the wall!
- Go around!

389
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:06,291
Hey! You!

390
00:27:07,375 --> 00:27:08,376
Stop right there!

391
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,131
Where the hell did he go?

392
00:27:13,214 --> 00:27:14,424
Where did he…

393
00:27:14,507 --> 00:27:15,550
- What the hell?
- Huh?

394
00:27:15,634 --> 00:27:16,676
Where did he go?

395
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:17,802
He came from there.

396
00:27:17,886 --> 00:27:21,139
- He's fast.
- You go this way. You, that way.

397
00:27:21,222 --> 00:27:22,599
- Move, you bastard!
- Damn it!

398
00:27:22,682 --> 00:27:23,933
For God's sake!

399
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:27,062
Man, he's fast.

400
00:27:27,145 --> 00:27:27,979
Spread out!

401
00:27:28,063 --> 00:27:29,064
- Yes, sir.
- Got it!

402
00:27:49,751 --> 00:27:51,586
Hey! Noja!

403
00:27:53,296 --> 00:27:54,130
Noja!

404
00:27:55,548 --> 00:27:56,549
Noja!

405
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:00,178
Noja!

406
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:02,514
Noja.

407
00:28:03,515 --> 00:28:04,683
Noja.

408
00:28:11,773 --> 00:28:12,899
Hey.

409
00:28:12,982 --> 00:28:15,110
You remember me, right?

410
00:28:18,863 --> 00:28:21,574
By the way, what do you do?

411
00:28:21,658 --> 00:28:23,076
Who the hell are you?

412
00:28:28,415 --> 00:28:29,791
Are you dead?

413
00:28:29,874 --> 00:28:31,418
Bastard, damn it.

414
00:29:23,678 --> 00:29:26,347
You can't even take a hit?

415
00:29:26,431 --> 00:29:27,807
Hey, what's your name?

416
00:29:27,891 --> 00:29:30,351
You said you didn't know Kim Yeong-geun,
you bastard.

417
00:29:30,435 --> 00:29:31,603
Where's Noja?

418
00:29:32,604 --> 00:29:33,521
Here.

419
00:29:36,316 --> 00:29:37,609
Fucking hell.

420
00:29:39,152 --> 00:29:42,447
You can't even take a hit?

421
00:29:47,118 --> 00:29:48,203
Hey.

422
00:29:48,703 --> 00:29:50,455
You can't even keep up?

423
00:29:52,874 --> 00:29:54,501
I don't have my glasses.

424
00:29:54,584 --> 00:29:57,086
For fuck's sake.

425
00:29:57,170 --> 00:29:59,047
Now I even have to babysit you?

426
00:30:00,465 --> 00:30:02,008
Fucking hell.

427
00:30:06,221 --> 00:30:07,430
Damn it.

428
00:30:07,514 --> 00:30:08,723
- Huh? Sir.
- My legs.

429
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:09,891
- I don't know.
- Here.

430
00:30:09,974 --> 00:30:10,809
Sir, wait.

431
00:30:11,434 --> 00:30:12,644
What the hell?

432
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:21,110
Why are you sitting there?

433
00:30:22,070 --> 00:30:23,655
Because I can't even take a hit.

434
00:30:25,281 --> 00:30:26,533
You got beaten up?

435
00:30:27,367 --> 00:30:29,327
- You actually got beaten up for once.
- Fuck.

436
00:30:29,410 --> 00:30:31,204
Someone give me a light. Quick.

437
00:30:31,287 --> 00:30:34,499
Put that away. Get up.
We're going to that bastard's office.

438
00:30:34,999 --> 00:30:36,084
Come on. Let's go.

439
00:30:36,793 --> 00:30:40,129
Fuck, give me a light or the key!

440
00:30:40,213 --> 00:30:42,298
- Are you kidding me?
- Dumbass.

441
00:30:42,799 --> 00:30:45,802
Wow, you're just so fucking great.

442
00:30:45,885 --> 00:30:46,970
- Damn it.
- Min-ho.

443
00:30:47,053 --> 00:30:48,346
- Yes?
- Aw, my legs.

444
00:30:49,681 --> 00:30:51,391
- Hey, hurry up.
- Okay.

445
00:30:53,601 --> 00:30:54,435
Oh Lord.

446
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:06,197
Jeez.

447
00:32:03,671 --> 00:32:04,714
You already know

448
00:32:05,214 --> 00:32:06,049
who I am.

449
00:32:11,387 --> 00:32:12,472
What?

450
00:32:15,308 --> 00:32:16,309
Panic attack again?

451
00:32:18,394 --> 00:32:19,854
I slipped.

452
00:32:49,008 --> 00:32:50,051
Huh?

453
00:32:50,134 --> 00:32:51,427
What's that?

454
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:53,805
What the hell?

455
00:32:55,556 --> 00:32:56,474
What is that?

456
00:33:08,319 --> 00:33:09,737
This is Dongbu Police Station.

457
00:33:11,364 --> 00:33:12,240
Okay.

458
00:33:14,909 --> 00:33:16,953
Okay. Got it.

459
00:33:18,162 --> 00:33:21,499
Sir. We just got a report of a body
in the Hangang River.

460
00:33:21,582 --> 00:33:23,668
- He's the abducted kid's father.
- What?

461
00:33:23,751 --> 00:33:25,003
Sir. Hurry. Get up.

462
00:33:25,086 --> 00:33:26,129
Yes, sir.

463
00:33:26,212 --> 00:33:27,463
Get ready to head out.

464
00:33:27,547 --> 00:33:28,423
Got it.

465
00:33:28,506 --> 00:33:30,258
What the fuck?

466
00:33:47,900 --> 00:33:48,735
Who?

467
00:33:48,818 --> 00:33:51,946
I'm Park Seung-gyu.
I used to work under Dong-seok.

468
00:33:55,199 --> 00:33:56,617
Come on.

469
00:33:56,701 --> 00:33:58,494
You really don't remember me.

470
00:33:59,746 --> 00:34:02,373
You seriously don't remember Dong-seok?

471
00:34:03,332 --> 00:34:07,378
You buried him on Mount Chilbo.

472
00:34:07,462 --> 00:34:08,463
I don't.

473
00:34:11,257 --> 00:34:12,717
You really don't remember me?

474
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:16,137
I even hired you a few times recently
to find people.

475
00:34:16,220 --> 00:34:19,015
How about Myeong-su?
You probably know him.

476
00:34:19,098 --> 00:34:20,391
He worked under Dong-seok.

477
00:34:20,475 --> 00:34:22,727
He killed someone
and fled to the Philippines.

478
00:34:22,810 --> 00:34:24,312
Don't know that punk either.

479
00:34:28,274 --> 00:34:30,860
Man, that kinda hurts.

480
00:34:30,943 --> 00:34:32,570
Just get to the point.

481
00:34:33,863 --> 00:34:35,615
Where are you coming from?

482
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:38,409
Oh.

483
00:34:39,452 --> 00:34:42,705
My girlfriend was whining about the pain,
so I went to get painkillers.

484
00:34:42,789 --> 00:34:43,998
Your girlfriend?

485
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:50,421
What, you suddenly into guys or something?

486
00:34:51,214 --> 00:34:53,299
I know everything. Damn it.

487
00:34:53,382 --> 00:34:55,760
Just tell me what you got yourself into.

488
00:34:55,843 --> 00:34:57,136
I'll help you.

489
00:34:57,220 --> 00:34:59,388
Hey, maybe you should take this.

490
00:35:00,515 --> 00:35:03,434
It works for headaches, toothaches,
and even menstrual cramps.

491
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:08,940
- You fucking--
- Hey, stop.

492
00:35:09,440 --> 00:35:10,775
Fuck.

493
00:35:11,275 --> 00:35:13,653
Hey. You fucker.

494
00:35:14,362 --> 00:35:17,657
When I say get to the point,
you get to the point.

495
00:35:17,740 --> 00:35:19,200
Noja.

496
00:35:20,535 --> 00:35:22,453
At this rate, we're all gonna die.

497
00:35:23,246 --> 00:35:26,499
While I'm asking nicely,
lay low for a bit.

498
00:35:27,875 --> 00:35:29,377
And if you're not asking nicely?

499
00:35:31,546 --> 00:35:35,424
The police had a tail on you.

500
00:35:37,051 --> 00:35:39,846
So I shook them for you.
I bet you didn't know that.

501
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:48,813
Where's the money you took from Dong-seok?

502
00:35:48,896 --> 00:35:51,274
The money you took when you betrayed him.

503
00:35:51,357 --> 00:35:54,777
The money we busted our asses for.

504
00:35:57,655 --> 00:36:01,367
Some bastard sent a tip,
and now we're all tangled up in this.

505
00:36:01,450 --> 00:36:05,079
We're all about to be fucked
because of you.

506
00:36:05,705 --> 00:36:09,792
At this fucking rate, Noja,
you might end up at Mount Chilbo.

507
00:36:24,223 --> 00:36:27,894
I need real tranquilizers,
not these pills.

508
00:36:27,977 --> 00:36:30,479
Pack your things already.
We have to go now.

509
00:36:30,563 --> 00:36:31,689
Why now?

510
00:36:31,772 --> 00:36:33,566
Just do what I say for once.

511
00:36:33,649 --> 00:36:35,026
What are you, a damn kid?

512
00:36:56,797 --> 00:36:57,757
Who is it?

513
00:37:17,068 --> 00:37:18,152
Who are you?

514
00:37:22,323 --> 00:37:23,157
Take

515
00:37:24,075 --> 00:37:25,076
this call.

516
00:37:27,954 --> 00:37:29,330
Not the big one.

517
00:37:31,165 --> 00:37:32,250
The skinny one.

518
00:37:44,178 --> 00:37:45,680
Speed dial one.

519
00:37:47,640 --> 00:37:49,267
Speed dial one.

520
00:38:06,993 --> 00:38:09,996
<i>I let the cat out</i>
<i>so it could catch the rat.</i>

521
00:38:10,079 --> 00:38:11,789
I guess you two are friends now, huh?

522
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:13,708
Who are you?

523
00:38:14,875 --> 00:38:15,793
<i>Huh?</i>

524
00:38:15,876 --> 00:38:17,628
You still don't know who I am?

525
00:38:18,129 --> 00:38:20,047
Hey, it's me.

526
00:38:21,257 --> 00:38:22,091
<i>You.</i>

527
00:38:23,467 --> 00:38:24,760
<i>If you wanna know who I am,</i>

528
00:38:25,553 --> 00:38:26,929
find yourself first.

529
00:38:27,430 --> 00:38:29,849
Find yourself first, you bastard.

530
00:38:30,850 --> 00:38:31,767
That rat bastard?

531
00:38:33,102 --> 00:38:35,896
Who is he calling a rat bastard?
You're the rat bastard.

532
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:38,566
<i>Police confirmed the body found</i>
<i>in the Hangang River…</i>

533
00:38:38,649 --> 00:38:40,526
<i>Wait, isn't that Soo-hyun?</i>

534
00:38:40,609 --> 00:38:42,695
<i>…is the father</i>
<i>of the abducted kindergartener.</i>

535
00:38:43,529 --> 00:38:45,072
I'm right. It's Soo-hyun.

536
00:38:45,656 --> 00:38:47,325
Hey, Soo-hyun's on TV.

537
00:38:47,408 --> 00:38:51,078
<i>Police have identified two suspects</i>
<i>and are tracking them.</i>

538
00:38:51,162 --> 00:38:53,789
<i>For more,</i>
<i>we go to our reporter at the scene.</i>

539
00:38:53,873 --> 00:38:57,960
<i>Yes, I'm at the Hangang River in Seoul,</i>
<i>where the body was found.</i>

540
00:38:58,044 --> 00:39:02,965
<i>A citizen reported a body floating</i>
<i>in the Hangang River this morning.</i>

541
00:39:03,049 --> 00:39:05,926
<i>The victim is the father</i>
<i>of the recently-abducted kindergartener</i>

542
00:39:06,010 --> 00:39:07,261
<i>who has since returned home.</i>

543
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:08,721
You fucking bastard.

544
00:39:08,804 --> 00:39:10,348
Why are you doing this?

545
00:39:10,431 --> 00:39:11,390
<i>What now?</i>

546
00:39:11,474 --> 00:39:13,142
The police are after you two.

547
00:39:13,225 --> 00:39:15,061
Just shut up and answer my question!

548
00:39:16,937 --> 00:39:18,939
Why the hell are you doing this?

549
00:39:21,692 --> 00:39:23,277
That's for you to find out.

550
00:39:23,986 --> 00:39:25,446
<i>I'll be waiting. Hurry.</i>

551
00:39:26,280 --> 00:39:27,740
I haven't got much time.

552
00:39:29,283 --> 00:39:30,326
See you again.

553
00:39:32,203 --> 00:39:35,581
<i>They are looking into his ties</i>
<i>to the suspects.</i>

554
00:39:35,664 --> 00:39:38,125
<i>The investigation is in its early stages,</i>

555
00:39:38,209 --> 00:39:40,628
<i>and all possibilities</i>
<i>are being considered.</i>

556
00:39:40,711 --> 00:39:45,758
<i>Police also urged the media</i>
<i>to avoid unverified rumors</i>

557
00:39:45,841 --> 00:39:48,511
<i>and sensational coverage of the case.</i>

558
00:39:48,594 --> 00:39:51,263
That fucking dumbass.

559
00:39:56,602 --> 00:39:57,937
Hey, we need to run.

560
00:39:58,437 --> 00:40:01,690
It's probably hacked.
Memorize the number and ditch it.

561
00:40:02,650 --> 00:40:04,902
Grab your clothes. For fuck's sake.

562
00:40:07,405 --> 00:40:10,491
TWO SUSPECTS IDENTIFIED AND BEING TRACKED

563
00:40:34,223 --> 00:40:35,516
<i>Soo-hyun!</i>

564
00:40:36,142 --> 00:40:36,976
<i>Damn it!</i>

565
00:40:37,059 --> 00:40:38,769
Soo-hyun, talk to me!

566
00:40:39,270 --> 00:40:40,146
Soo-hyun!

567
00:40:52,199 --> 00:40:54,160
They say it shows signs of suicide.

568
00:40:56,704 --> 00:41:00,249
His daughter was kidnapped.
You think suicide makes sense?

569
00:41:00,332 --> 00:41:01,167
It doesn't.

570
00:41:03,210 --> 00:41:04,962
"Was not a suicide."

571
00:41:05,045 --> 00:41:06,839
That's what the tip said as well.

572
00:41:08,340 --> 00:41:10,593
And he was the landlord,

573
00:41:11,093 --> 00:41:13,387
and the bastard living there
is the kidnapper.

574
00:41:15,139 --> 00:41:18,601
Fuck. Where do I even start?

575
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:24,315
I don't know.

576
00:41:26,066 --> 00:41:27,902
You were taken to Noja's agency,

577
00:41:27,985 --> 00:41:30,154
then dragged out by two thugs.

578
00:41:30,237 --> 00:41:32,573
Your address was on Noja's computer.

579
00:41:33,199 --> 00:41:34,408
I don't know anything.

580
00:41:42,041 --> 00:41:43,876
I'm not here to bust you for gambling.

581
00:41:43,959 --> 00:41:47,755
I'm not interested in you.
I just need to get this bastard. Hey.

582
00:41:48,255 --> 00:41:49,465
Hey.

583
00:41:50,174 --> 00:41:53,302
I'll fucking get them for you.
Just tell me if you know this bastard.

584
00:41:55,095 --> 00:41:56,597
Even if I did, I can't say.

585
00:41:58,349 --> 00:42:00,935
I could end up
as fucking unclaimed remains.

586
00:42:09,568 --> 00:42:12,112
Those bastards are all in it together.

587
00:42:12,196 --> 00:42:15,282
They lend you money for gambling.
If you run, they come get you.

588
00:42:15,366 --> 00:42:17,952
It's either your identity or your organs.
Detective.

589
00:42:20,162 --> 00:42:21,747
Detective, what would you sell?

590
00:42:22,790 --> 00:42:25,709
They steal identities
from the homeless and those in debt.

591
00:42:25,793 --> 00:42:28,462
If things go south,
they kill them and stage it as a suicide.

592
00:42:28,546 --> 00:42:31,257
So don't ever come looking for me.

593
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:33,050
I've got nothing left but my life.

594
00:42:34,426 --> 00:42:36,303
Hey.

595
00:43:00,536 --> 00:43:02,162
A man died.

596
00:43:02,788 --> 00:43:04,665
He just jumped off the bridge.

597
00:43:06,208 --> 00:43:09,545
Anyway, because of Noja,
cops will be everywhere.

598
00:43:10,462 --> 00:43:13,507
That bastard's not as sharp
as he used to be.

599
00:43:16,552 --> 00:43:18,053
It's not just his problem.

600
00:43:18,137 --> 00:43:20,806
The pigs were onto me,
so I had to move my operation.

601
00:43:20,889 --> 00:43:24,518
So you gotta help me out here.

602
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:25,811
How?

603
00:43:28,439 --> 00:43:29,398
Noja.

604
00:43:29,481 --> 00:43:31,525
Gotta deal with him
before the cops get to us.

605
00:43:31,609 --> 00:43:34,612
I tried to talk to him,
but nothing fucking got through.

606
00:43:35,654 --> 00:43:37,573
Get some guys to take care of Noja.

607
00:43:37,656 --> 00:43:39,158
We need to bury both bastards.

608
00:43:40,075 --> 00:43:42,202
I've been living like this lately too.

609
00:43:42,286 --> 00:43:44,121
I don't really have anyone to call.

610
00:43:46,582 --> 00:43:47,833
That's your problem.

611
00:43:48,417 --> 00:43:50,419
Wanna keep your hands fucking clean, huh?

612
00:43:50,502 --> 00:43:54,089
We're in this together.
Don't act like it's not your problem.

613
00:43:54,173 --> 00:43:55,382
Fuck, I…

614
00:43:55,883 --> 00:43:59,303
I'm only asking nicely because it's you.

615
00:43:59,386 --> 00:44:01,263
Who gave you that identity?

616
00:44:01,347 --> 00:44:02,973
I did, didn't I?

617
00:44:03,057 --> 00:44:04,516
When you were on the run,

618
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:07,061
everyone thought
you were fucking in the Philippines.

619
00:44:07,144 --> 00:44:09,605
Bullshit. You've never fucking been there.

620
00:44:12,024 --> 00:44:15,861
- I mean, I do appreciate that--
- What about this place?

621
00:44:15,944 --> 00:44:18,280
Who got you a job so you could get by?

622
00:44:19,073 --> 00:44:21,659
Is this fucking business yours?!

623
00:44:22,701 --> 00:44:26,497
Hey, you fucking bastard!
You're just the front! Act like one!

624
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:34,963
Myeong-su.

625
00:44:36,298 --> 00:44:38,759
You're just here to take the hit for me.

626
00:44:41,762 --> 00:44:43,847
You're fucking nothing.

627
00:44:45,724 --> 00:44:49,436
Just say yes when I ask nicely.

628
00:44:52,147 --> 00:44:53,148
I'll try to find some.

629
00:44:57,903 --> 00:44:59,029
I'll find some.

630
00:45:06,078 --> 00:45:06,912
But you know,

631
00:45:06,995 --> 00:45:10,124
this has nothing to do with me, okay?

632
00:45:10,874 --> 00:45:11,875
I know.

633
00:45:22,636 --> 00:45:25,556
And run the site better.

634
00:45:25,639 --> 00:45:26,765
Boost the odds a bit.

635
00:45:26,849 --> 00:45:30,477
That's how you get
those little bastards swarming in.

636
00:45:30,561 --> 00:45:31,520
Okay?

637
00:45:32,896 --> 00:45:33,814
Okay.

638
00:45:36,400 --> 00:45:37,526
Hey, Mr. Kwak!

639
00:45:37,609 --> 00:45:38,986
Lend me some money.

640
00:45:39,737 --> 00:45:42,823
Damn, I'm running cold today.

641
00:45:44,700 --> 00:45:46,785
Sir. I'll head out now.

642
00:45:46,869 --> 00:45:48,036
Yeah, sure.

643
00:45:48,120 --> 00:45:49,163
Sir.

644
00:46:03,385 --> 00:46:06,054
The cards just aren't going my way.

645
00:46:06,138 --> 00:46:09,558
The flow keeps breaking,
and my timing's been off all day.

646
00:46:10,058 --> 00:46:14,104
It may not look like much,
but it's been fully serviced.

647
00:46:14,188 --> 00:46:15,773
It's a great car, Noja.

648
00:46:15,856 --> 00:46:17,149
What do you drive?

649
00:46:17,232 --> 00:46:18,859
Me? I drive…

650
00:46:20,277 --> 00:46:21,320
Over there.

651
00:46:22,404 --> 00:46:23,405
Nice.

652
00:46:24,531 --> 00:46:25,365
Swap with me.

653
00:46:26,283 --> 00:46:29,828
- Noja, the price of that car is--
- I'm heading out of town.

654
00:46:30,704 --> 00:46:31,705
- Huh?
- Keys.

655
00:46:32,956 --> 00:46:34,082
Noja.

656
00:46:34,583 --> 00:46:35,542
Come on, Noja!

657
00:46:35,626 --> 00:46:39,171
I finally went all out
and had the whole car reconditioned.

658
00:46:39,254 --> 00:46:41,006
Come on!

659
00:46:42,549 --> 00:46:43,425
Keys.

660
00:46:46,178 --> 00:46:47,429
Goddamn it.

661
00:46:48,597 --> 00:46:49,640
This is…

662
00:47:03,403 --> 00:47:05,447
No name on that rat bastard's number.

663
00:47:05,531 --> 00:47:06,949
It's a burner phone.

664
00:47:07,032 --> 00:47:08,826
This is a burner phone too. Use it.

665
00:47:08,909 --> 00:47:11,203
Don't call or text anyone.
Only use it with me.

666
00:47:14,414 --> 00:47:15,499
Hey, is that the one?

667
00:47:15,582 --> 00:47:17,543
Yeah, it is. How did you get it?

668
00:47:18,377 --> 00:47:21,463
You can get drugs delivered these days.
This is nothing.

669
00:47:22,047 --> 00:47:23,298
By the way,

670
00:47:24,424 --> 00:47:26,134
why do you wear fake glasses?

671
00:47:26,635 --> 00:47:28,345
I just feel more at ease.

672
00:47:28,428 --> 00:47:30,973
You're a weird little bastard, aren't you?

673
00:47:31,056 --> 00:47:33,642
What, is it like a mask?

674
00:47:35,310 --> 00:47:36,395
Why would I wear one?

675
00:47:37,020 --> 00:47:38,981
That's what guilty bastards do.

676
00:47:39,064 --> 00:47:41,817
They keep hiding things,
covering them up, and changing them.

677
00:47:43,819 --> 00:47:45,279
So, have you thought about it?

678
00:47:51,201 --> 00:47:53,287
I'm starving. Fuck, let's go eat.

679
00:48:18,103 --> 00:48:18,937
Moon-jae!

680
00:48:21,148 --> 00:48:22,065
Moon-jae!

681
00:48:23,734 --> 00:48:24,860
I think I know him.

682
00:48:29,239 --> 00:48:30,073
Who is he?

683
00:48:42,252 --> 00:48:43,503
Aren't you getting in?

684
00:48:56,516 --> 00:48:58,727
Spit it out, punk. Who the hell is he?

685
00:49:01,563 --> 00:49:03,857
I knew him at university.

686
00:49:03,941 --> 00:49:05,776
He was kinda like, you know…

687
00:49:06,568 --> 00:49:08,320
He really envied me.

688
00:49:09,613 --> 00:49:10,447
Jealous, I guess.

689
00:49:11,448 --> 00:49:12,741
Jealous?

690
00:49:12,824 --> 00:49:13,659
Not a grudge?

691
00:49:16,203 --> 00:49:17,204
No.

692
00:49:18,580 --> 00:49:19,831
It wasn't like that.

693
00:49:22,542 --> 00:49:26,004
If it's not a grudge,
why the fuck is he pulling this shit?

694
00:49:27,464 --> 00:49:28,632
No idea.

695
00:49:28,715 --> 00:49:30,884
But I can't shake the feeling it's him.

696
00:49:31,551 --> 00:49:33,720
Really? Then we should run with it.

697
00:49:42,437 --> 00:49:44,272
That'll be 228,000 won.

698
00:50:29,067 --> 00:50:30,736
Where do we go to get that bastard?

699
00:50:30,819 --> 00:50:31,737
An island.

700
00:50:33,155 --> 00:50:34,114
An island?

701
00:50:41,747 --> 00:50:42,998
Where?

702
00:50:47,544 --> 00:50:49,296
VINTORA STEAKHOUSE
118,000 WON APPROVED

703
00:50:53,341 --> 00:50:54,176
Hey.

704
00:50:56,678 --> 00:50:57,554
What the hell?

705
00:55:59,022 --> 00:56:01,941
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
